topaz: 4K pages experiment (let the four Cortex-A53 Silver cores run)

The Silver Cortex-A53 cores have no 16K translation granule
(ID_AA64MMFR0.TGran16 = 0), which is why the port runs on the four Gold
cores only. A 4K-page kernel can run on all eight.

The 16K-built iOS 16.7.16 userland maps fine under a 4K kernel: its
segments are 16K-aligned, which is a superset of 4K, and XNU arm64
supports both granules (watchOS builds this way).

THIS IS AN EXPERIMENT: the kernel is expected to compile; booting may
still fail on port assumptions (physmap padding, commpage layout) that
were written for 16K. Test with `fastboot boot` only (RAM image).
---
 pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h | 6 ++-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)-2 additions

diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 #define __ARM_ENABLE_SWAP__       1
 #define __ARM_V8_CRYPTO_EXTENSIONS__ 1
 /* topaz: Cortex-A53/A73 have no PAN (ARMv8.1); MSR PAN is undefined there */
-#define __ARM_16K_PG__            1
+#define __ARM_4K_PG__             1
 
 #define HAS_GIC_V3                1
 
